                        "glosses": [
                            "A noun which only occurs in one case."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "49f9e221-a06a-4b25-9ee8-06a0afb9254f",
                                "sense_id": "54d449f9-aa3f-3772-8579-fd0fa016b531",
                                "text": "A noun which is found in one case only, is called a Monoptote; if found in two cases, a Diptote; if in three, a Triptote; if in four, a Tetraptote; and if in five, a Pentaptote."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7647c6c-6e54-45ec-a145-b26faba1a044",
                                "sense_id": "54d449f9-aa3f-3772-8579-fd0fa016b531",
                                "text": "What is meant by monoptote, diptote, and triptote nouns? Give examples.\nA monoptote is a noun which has only one case, as natu; a diptote two, as fors, forte; a triptote three, as opis, opem, ope."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
